Description: Deliver mesh packets to the HTTP web UI after a reboot without a new want_config.
 Saving LoRa config reboots meshtasticd. The browser keeps polling
 /api/v1/fromradio while PhoneAPI is still STATE_SEND_NOTHING, so
 available() returned false and chat stayed empty even though Router
 had the text.
 Register HTTP clients in phoneClients during STATE_SEND_NOTHING so they
 receive per-client fanout copies even when another PhoneAPI client (e.g.
 TCP port 4403) is active. Disconnect HTTP client after 30 seconds of
 polling inactivity to prevent stale packet buildup.
Author: Roy C. Gross <61633595+radioroy@users.noreply.github.com>
Origin: other
Forwarded: no
Applies-to: meshtastic/firmware @ 54e0d8d0ab2ff56b3a9ce967e53f79e49af560fb (after 0004)
